According to the rule, "Every top-level balanced object in the text is a candidate, not only the span from the first { to the last }" and "The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text". Thus for input with two top-level objects, the recovered object is the last one, {"b":2}, same as rewritten with only that object, so the check's answer ought to be unchanged.